RulesError Display, per variant (DA.16 pins each): Parse / Invalid - one diagnostic per line, in source order; Budget - the sentence below; Builtin - ``builtin `<name>` failed: <message>``; Type - `<message>` (the message names the predicate, e.g. ``sum over a non-integer value in `w/2` ``); Unknown - ``unknown output `<predicate>`; the program defines <known, comma-separated, sorted>``. Diagnostic Display omits the ` (in the rule for ..)` suffix when `predicate` is None (lexical errors).
Budget's Display is the actionable text DA.14b and DB print verbatim: "rule evaluation stopped: `tc/2` (rules:3) reached 5000000 derived rows, the row budget. Its recursion is probably unseeded: bind an argument from a small relation (`tc(x, y) :- seed(x), ...`), use reaches(x, y, \"CATS\") for reachability, or raise the budget." No thiserror (the crate has no external dependency): Display and Error by hand.

