Interning: strings are stored once (the map key is a 64-bit std DefaultHasher digest - fixed keys, so deterministic - with a collision chain through `next`), so a qname attribute column does not hold every qname twice. Handle order is interning order, which is deterministic for a given FactSource order but NOT checkout-stable; it is used only inside relations (joins, dedup), never for output order. cmp_rendered is the one output order: type rank Int < Str < Node, then Int numeric, Str by bytes, Node by its rendered key (FactSource::render_node, DA.6) and, only when two nodes render identically, by NodeId (documented as the single non-checkout-stable tie, reached only when a domain renders two nodes the same). Lookup's inner map is a private tuple field, so no module but value.rs can reach it; DA.19's source guard pins that value.rs never iterates it (a compile_fail doc test cannot name a pub(crate) type from outside the crate, so it would pass vacuously).

