A private `PredGraph { nodes: Vec<NodeId>, edges: Vec<Edge> }` implements GraphSource with NodeId(p as u64) for p in 0..npreds and Edge::new(NodeId(body), NodeId(head), EdgeCategoryId(0 | 1 | 2 for Pos | Neg | Agg), Confidence::Strong) in input order; Adjacency::build(&g, &CategorySet::all()); strongly_connected gives the non-trivial components (members sorted by value = predicate index = first-definition order); every other predicate is its own component. A Neg or Agg edge whose two ends share a component (a self edge included) makes that component a BadCycle - one per component, preds ascending, the dep and site of its first offending edge in input order; every BadCycle is returned (analysis words them, DA.5b). Strata: the condensation in topological order by Kahn's algorithm over components, the ready set kept sorted by smallest member (a sorted Vec, never a hash map), so a predicate's stratum is a function of the program text; each component is one stratum, so every Neg / Agg edge crosses strata upward. No HashMap, no recursion (iterative Tarjan in activation, a queue here).

