Checks, each an Error Diagnostic at the offending span naming the rule's head `name/arity`: (a) unknown predicate - used in a body, never a head, not EDB / attribute / builtin - with `did you mean `x`?` (Levenshtein <= 2 over every known name, ties by name); (b) arity mismatch across uses or against a declaration (both sites named); (c) a head defining an EDB, attribute or builtin name; a user name starting `__` (reserved for synthetic predicates; allowed only under allow_synthetic); (d) typed constants: a Str in a Kind / Category / CellType column must be a registry name (`unknown node kind `ROTUE`; did you mean `ROUTE`?`), a CategorySet constant parses as `*`, or `A|B|..` of registered names (the carry set when the builtin has no category argument), an Int column takes an Int literal, a Const-bound builtin argument must be a literal; (e) safety: every head variable, every variable of a negated atom or comparison (except `_`, and except one side of an Eq whose other side is bound - an assignment), and every aggregated variable is bound by a positive relation atom, a May column of a builtin, or an assignment; a Must builtin column must be bound before the call can run (checked against sips_order); a fact (empty body) has no variables; `_` in a head is an error; (f) aggregates: a predicate with an aggregate head has exactly that one rule, its group terms are variables or constants, and it is not recursive; (g) stratification: one DepEdge per body literal that names an IDB predicate (Pos / Neg; Agg for every positive body atom of an aggregate rule) goes to strata::stratify (DA.5a); each BadCycle becomes one Error at its site listing the component's predicates sorted by name; strata, recursive flags and components come from its Strata. Warnings: (h) singleton variable (`variable `y` appears once; write `_``); (i) unseeded recursion - a recursive SCC none of whose base rules (rules with no atom of the SCC) has a constant argument, a lower-stratum IDB atom or a builtin call with a Const / Must constant - message `recursive predicate `tc/2` is unseeded: its recursion starts from every row of `edge/3`; seed it (`tc(x, y) :- seed(x), ...`) or use reaches(x, y, "CATS"); magic sets seed it when every caller binds an argument (DA.12)`. negated_reads: for each negated atom, the edge categories its predicate reads transitively - constant categories of edge / edge_conf / edge_cell atoms and the category set of every reaches / scc call in its defining cone (the carry set expands to the carry names, `*` and any non-constant category set any_category) - the static absence caveats Q5 attaches to rows (DA.14b). sips_order: greedy - next is `first` if given; else any literal whose columns are all bound (a pure filter: membership atoms, comparisons, negations, fully bound builtins) in source order; else the literal with the most bound columns (constants and bound vars), ties to the smaller known size (EDB / lower-stratum sizes the caller passes; unknown = usize::MAX), then source order; a builtin whose Must columns are not yet bound is not eligible. No HashMap iteration (name -> PredId uses value::Lookup; predicate lists are Vecs in first-seen order).

MESSAGE TABLE (the exact texts; DA.16 pins them end to end and DB's check / gaps print them): unknown predicate ``unknown predicate `edg/3`; did you mean `edge`?`` (no suggestion when none is within distance 2); arity ``predicate `p` is used with 2 arguments here but defined with 1``; unknown names ``unknown node kind `ROTUE`; did you mean `ROUTE`?``, ``unknown edge category `CALS`; did you mean `CALLS`?``, ``unknown cell type `X` ``, ``unknown edge category `NOPE` in the category set `CALLS|NOPE` ``; reserved heads ```edge/3` is a built-in predicate and cannot be defined by a rule``, ``predicate names starting `__` are reserved``; constants ``argument 4 of `reaches/4` must be an integer literal``, ``argument 3 of `reaches/3` must be a quoted category set``; safety ``variable `y` in the head of `v/1` is not bound by the body``, ``variable `x` in the negated atom `p/1` is not bound by a positive atom``, ``variable `y` in a comparison is not bound by a positive atom``, ```_` may not appear in a head``, ```in_scope/2` needs argument 2 bound before the call``; aggregates ```fan/2` has an aggregate head, so it must have exactly one rule (found 2)``, ``aggregated variable `x` of `fan/2` is not bound by the body``; strata ``negation inside recursion: `p/0`, `q/0` depend on each other through this negated atom``, ``aggregation inside recursion: `p/1` depends on itself through this aggregate``; warnings ``variable `y` appears once; write `_` `` and the unseeded-recursion text above.

