insert_round: sort to_add (with metas) by (row, height, rule) and dedup by row, keeping the lowest height and then the lowest rule index (a checkout-stable choice: heights and rule indexes are properties of the program and data, not of ids); drop every row already present at ANY level (gallop through each sorted batch of the identity index - to_add is sorted, so this is a merge); push the survivors as the level's `recent` in every index (each index sorts its own permuted copy). advance(): recent becomes a stable run; trailing runs merge while the earlier run is no more than twice the later (datafrog's geometric merge, so a part holds O(log n) runs). Cursor.seek gallops forward from the previous position in every run when keys arrive in non-decreasing order (the merge-join path when the outer scan is sorted on the key) and falls back to binary search otherwise; a key is a prefix of the index's permuted columns. View filters by level range, run kind and (explain) height < max_height. contains / exists_prefix look across all parts. Memory per tuple per index: arity x 4 + 6 bytes (heights u32 + rules u16 as separate vectors) + 4 for EDB ordinals on the identity index only. Row counting (len) feeds DA.14b's budget.

