Index per category set, built on first use: CatSet::Carry -> tables.carry_edges, All -> CategorySet::all(), Of(v) -> CategorySet::of(v); `Adjacency::build(src, &set)`; then one pass over src.edges() with the same category filter fills kept_level (tier.level()) and kept_ordinal in kept order - the order Adjacency::build keeps (global edge order filtered by category), asserted equal to adj.kept_edges() in length (a mismatch returns no rows and counts an error in stats, never panics). Semantics: reaches(x, y) holds when y is reachable from x by ONE OR MORE hops of the set's categories - the transitive closure `+` (CodeQL's `+`, GQL's `->{1,}`), so (x, x) holds exactly when x is on a cycle and the builtin agrees row for row with the recursive `tc` rules (DA.18); reaches/4 bounds the hop count to 1..=depth. reach_from / reach: bfs_levels(adj, seeds, kept_level, LevelWalk{walk: Forward | Backward, levels: 3, plus: true, max_depth: depth or usize::MAX}) -> (id, Tier::from_level(level)) for every reached node (a seed is a row only when a >= 1-hop walk reaches it; rows in walk order; DA.14b sorts). reach is memoised per (set, source, direction, depth) in a Lookup (looked up, never iterated); every memo row counts toward exec's budget (DA.14a) through stats. scc_rows: comps = strongly_connected(&adj) (full graph, every tier); rank members by FactSource::render_node then NodeId; rep = the first; a member x's tier = max(level of rep -> x, level of x -> rep) from two plus-mode bfs_levels walks from rep (Forward and Backward) with `within` = the component mask, so each walk stays inside the component (a path between two members of an SCC never leaves it) and costs O(component); rep's own row (rep, rep) takes the forward plus-walk's level of rep itself - the best tier of a cycle through rep, which also covers a one-node self-loop component. path: rank array = dense indices ordered by rendered key (computed once per set, lazily, only on explain), one-level walk (edge levels mapped to 0 when <= level else u8::MAX), parent_rank Some(rank); follow parents from target back to a seed, mapping kept_edge -> global ordinal and tier. cycle: path(rep -> x) + path(x -> rep) inside the component mask; for x == rep, the ranked walk from rep plus the lowest-ranked member u at minimal depth with an edge u -> rep at <= level (scan of the kept edges into rep). Canonical hops: the parent chain fixes the nodes, but two parallel edges between one parent and child (CALLS and USES, say) would otherwise be chosen by edge order, which a re-salted checkout reverses. So each CatIndex lazily keeps `pairs: Vec<(u32 from_ix, u32 to_ix, u32 kept)>` sorted (built on the first path / cycle request, one pass plus one sort, explain-time only), and every hop is the kept edge between its two nodes, walkable at the level, with the smallest (tier level, category NAME, ordinal); cycle()'s edges into rep come from a second lazily sorted copy keyed by to_ix. Ordinal only breaks ties between same-key edges (two call sites), whose rendered hop is identical. Hop.ordinal is the GLOBAL edge ordinal DB maps back to its &Edge for EVIDENCE. Stats feed DA.14b's `[rules] closure` line.

