vacuous (`!in_scope(f, "legacy")` holds for every node). Trial::measure(text, probe) memoises by text as today (the probe only matters for WITH, whose text differs from BASE's unless every stanza is a duplicate). LEAVE-ONE-OUT: WITHOUT(s) is built for every non-constraint stanza only. A [[constraint]] stanza adds a CONSTRAINT cell on an existing anchor node and nothing else, so its WITHOUT graph has WITH's counts and gap ids exactly: its `marginal` is GraphDelta::default(), `closes` empty, and no build is spent on it - `builds` counts at most 2 + the graph stanzas. DELTA: `RulesDelta::between(before: Option<&RuleState>, after: Option<&RuleState>)` (None = no rules): added = after's keys not in before (BTreeMap order: rule_id, kind, key), resolved = the reverse, each list cut at MAX_RULE_HITS with the totals counting all, blocking = the added hits with blocking, errors = after's errors whose id before lacks, sorted by id. RULE TRIAL (each [[constraint]] stanza r, id = r.key, judged on BASE and WITH): status = RULE_DUPLICATE when merge placed it Location::AlreadyPresent or BASE's state declares a rule with that id (a cell-API rule, or an anchored base stanza); else RULE_ERROR when WITH's errors hold the id (`error` = the message, newlines flattened to "; "); else RULE_ORPHANED when WITH's ids lack it (no `anchor` and no PROJECT at its scope, or an anchor qname that binds nothing: no CONSTRAINT cell, so `glia check` never reads it); else RULE_VIOLATED when WITH holds any hit with that rule_id, else RULE_HOLDS. violations / tiers / blocking / hits (cut at MAX_RULE_HITS) count WITH's hits of that rule; empty_scopes from WITH's probe. VERDICTS, written into the module doc as a table: `rule_verdict(t)` = KEEP for holds with no empty scope (it holds on the code as it is; `glia check` keeps it true from now on); REVIEW for holds with an empty scope (it may pass vacuously: a misspelt scope, or one meant to stay empty) and for violated (the rule or the code is wrong; `blocking