/// Disjoint sets over dense indices 0..n. The root of a set is always its SMALLEST index (union links the larger
/// root under the smaller), so with indices assigned in NodeId order the representative is the minimum NodeId.
pub struct UnionFind { parent: Vec<u32> }
impl UnionFind {
  pub fn new(n: usize) -> Self;            // n > u32::MAX: an empty set (LD.15's cap), never a panic
  pub fn find(&mut self, i: u32) -> u32;   // iterative two-pass full path compression
  pub fn union(&mut self, a: u32, b: u32) -> u32; // returns the surviving root = min(find(a), find(b))
  pub fn len(&self) -> usize; pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool;
}
/// Equivalence classes of NodeIds, only classes of two or more members kept.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Classes { ids: Vec<NodeId> /* every member, sorted by .0 */, rep_of: Vec<u32> /* index into ids of
  each member's representative */, classes: Vec<(NodeId, Vec<NodeId>)> /* (rep, members asc) sorted by rep */ }
impl Classes {
  pub fn from_pairs<I: IntoIterator<Item = (NodeId, NodeId)>>(pairs: I) -> Self;
  pub fn from_source<G: GraphSource + ?Sized>(g: &G, keep: &CategorySet, filter: impl Fn(&Edge) -> bool) -> Self;
  pub fn rep(&self, id: NodeId) -> NodeId;            // the class minimum; `id` itself when in no class
  pub fn class_of(&self, id: NodeId) -> Option<&[NodeId]>; // the members, ascending
  pub fn same(&self, a: NodeId, b: NodeId) -> bool;
  pub fn classes(&self) -> impl Iterator<Item = (NodeId, &[NodeId])> + '_; // by rep ascending
  pub fn len(&self) -> usize /* classes */; pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool; pub fn members(&self) -> usize;
}
/// `inner` with every class contracted to its representative.
pub struct Quotient<'g, G: GraphSource + ?Sized> { inner: &'g G, classes: &'g Classes, nodes: Vec<NodeId>,
  edges: Vec<Edge>, collapsed: usize }
impl<'g, G: GraphSource + ?Sized> Quotient<'g, G> {
  pub fn new(inner: &'g G, classes: &'g Classes) -> Self;
  pub fn rep(&self, id: NodeId) -> NodeId; pub fn collapsed_edges(&self) -> usize; pub fn inner(&self) -> &'g G;
}
impl<G: GraphSource + ?Sized> GraphSource for Quotient<'_, G> { /* node_ids: self.nodes.clone(); edges: self.edges.iter() */ }
```
from_pairs: collect every endpoint of every pair with a != b, sort + dedup by .0 (the dense order IS NodeId order, so the min-index root is the min NodeId), union each pair by binary-searched indices, then one pass finds every root, groups members by root (members already ascending because indices are), drops singletons, and records rep_of. No HashMap anywhere: lookups are binary searches over the sorted `ids`, so nothing depends on hash order. A pair (a, a) and a repeated pair change nothing. from_source walks g.edges() once, keeping an edge whose category `keep` contains and that `filter` accepts, and calls from_pairs. Quotient::new walks inner.edges() once in order: each endpoint maps through classes.rep; an edge whose ORIGINAL endpoints differ but map to one rep is dropped and counted in `collapsed` (an intra-class edge: the SAME_AS star itself, or a SHARES_SCHEMA edge between two members of one class - the double-walk R2 section 11 names); a genuine self-loop (from == to before mapping) is kept; every other edge is pushed as Edge::new(rep(from), rep(to), category, confidence) WITHOUT cells (walks and PPR read endpoints, category and confidence only, and cloning EVIDENCE cells per query would cost O(E) allocations). Edge order is the inner order (Adjacency parity rule 2 holds over the quotient). node_ids: inner.node_ids() mapped through rep, first occurrence kept. With empty classes the quotient's node_ids and the (from, to, category, confidence) of its edges equal the inner graph's. Dense indices are u32 (LD.15's cap): an input over u32::MAX ids yields empty Classes. The module doc states the min-id representative is an internal handle, never an identity to show (R2 risk: it moves when a RepoId changes); the persisted SAME_AS stars choose their center by content instead (DD.5).

